secubox-mitmproxy (1.0.5-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * fix(waf): mitmproxy-11 upstream routing (#603). The addon only redirected
    the upstream in the `request` hook, but mitmproxy 11 opens the upstream
    connection between `requestheaders` and `request` — so routed vhosts
    connected to their public DNS IP instead of the internal backend (the WAF
    was effectively pass-through). Added a `requestheaders` hook that sets
    `flow.server_conn.address` before the connect. Ported from the live gk2
    fix that restored apt.secubox.in + all inspected vhosts.

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Mon, 15 Jun 2026 16:00:00 +0200

secubox-mitmproxy (1.0.4-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Pre-route SELF_HOSTS guard. When a client targets the box by
    literal local IP (192.168.1.200, 10.100.0.1, 10.55.0.1, etc.) and
    the Host is NOT in haproxy-routes.json, the v1.0.3 loop guard
    correctly broke the runaway but the user saw a 508 page. The new
    pre-route check in request() rewrites unmapped self-IP Hosts to
    nginx 9080 BEFORE forwarding, so the canonical hub vhost answers
    instead. The 508 path now only fires as a true last resort and
    logs the offending Host so the route can be added.

 -- Gerald Kerma <devel@cybermind.fr>  Sun, 24 May 2026 09:10:00 +0200

secubox-mitmproxy (1.0.3-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=high

  * Self-loop guard in secubox_waf.py request() hook. When the X-Forwarded-For
    chain contains mitmproxy's own LXC IP (10.100.0.60) more than twice, the
    WAF short-circuits with 508 Loop Detected instead of forwarding upstream.
    Stops runaway CPU when a Host header (eg literal IP from Eye Remote at
    10.55.0.1) is not in haproxy-routes.json and would otherwise bounce
    through HAProxy default_backend mitmproxy_inspector forever — observed
    on gk2 with mitmdump at sustained 84% CPU and ~50 XFF self-references
    per request.

 -- Gerald Kerma <devel@cybermind.fr>  Fri, 23 May 2026 14:30:00 +0200

secubox-mitmproxy (1.0.2-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * /data convention migration (#319 Phase 1). All hardcoded /srv/<pkg>
    paths in source replaced by /data/<pkg> (canonical SecuBox storage
    per charter §Storage). debian/postinst gains an idempotent migration
    block that moves legacy /srv/<dir> → /data/<dir> on upgrade and
    leaves a symlink behind for back-compat.

 -- Gerald Kerma <devel@cybermind.fr>  Thu, 21 May 2026 14:30:00 +0000

